# .dockerignore -- scopes the Docker build context for src/relay/Dockerfile (dist RP4), whose
# build context is the REPO ROOT (the relay crate is a workspace member; see that Dockerfile's own
# header comment for why). Default-deny, then allow back exactly what a Rust image build needs.
# Without this, `docker build -f src/relay/Dockerfile .` would tar the ~2.5k files of C++/Python/
# RE-doc tree that make up the rest of this monorepo -- correct either way (BuildKit only actually
# TRANSFERS what a COPY instruction references), but this makes the context-walk itself cheap and
# is the belt to that suspenders.
#
# src/collector's own image builds with `context: src/collector` (its own directory is already
# self-contained -- see src/collector/Dockerfile) and so is UNAFFECTED by this file: Docker only
# honours a `.dockerignore` located at the build context's own root, not this repo-root one.
*
!Cargo.toml
!Cargo.lock
!rust-toolchain.toml
!src/relay
!src/relay/**
!src/launcher
!src/launcher/**
